#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""b70: serve large MoE models on an Intel Arc Pro B70 (32 GB) with a RAM tier and an NVMe expert store.

    b70 setup [glm|sglang|dsv41|all]       one-time, CPU only: unpack the SGLang XPU image, fetch and build the kernels
    b70 info <model dir>                   JSON: which family the model is, whether setup and prepare are done
    b70 prepare <model dir> [--store DIR]  one-time per model: pack the NVMe expert store (GLM, DSV4.1; Flash-Next
                                           fills its own)
    b70 serve <model dir> --port N [--ctx N] [--parallel N] [--name NAME] [--store DIR] [--all-ram] [--prepare]
                                           OpenAI-compatible server in the foreground; SIGTERM stops it
    b70 run glm|sglang|dsv41 <command...>  run a command in an install's sandbox, without the GPU
    b70 stop                               stop a running `b70 serve`
    b70 status                             JSON: the running server, if any

Families (by config.json model_type), and the install that serves them:
  gemma      Gemma 4 EXL3 (gemma4): sglang, drafting with Google's assistant model (--drafter)
  flashnext  Qwen3.8-Flash-Next EXL3 (qwen4_exp): sglang, experts in VRAM, RAM and an NVMe store
  glm        GLM-5.3-Flash EXL3 (glm5_next): glm/ (exllamav3 fork + B70 tier), one request at a time
  dsv41      DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash EXL3 (deepseek_v41): dsv41/ (vcruz305's exllamav3 fork + dsv41/exllamav3.patch, the GLM
             install's kernels, its own B70 tier), one request at a time, drafting with the model's own DSpark blocks
The sglang install is SGLang 0.5.20-xpu with 0xSero's trellis-serve (EXL3 kernels for Intel) and trellis-serve.patch.

Everything runs inside the unpacked lmsysorg/sglang XPU image through bubblewrap; no Docker, no root. `serve` and
`run --gpu` take their turn on the B70 through the b70q queue (~/ai/b70q) when its daemon runs: they wait in line, then
hold the card; a server (--queue OWNER, --idle DUR) is stopped by the queue after DUR idle on the GPU while another job
waits. `serve` is also a guard: it stops the server at the first xe fault on the B70 or when RAM runs low, and does not
start beside a Steam game that has the B70 open.

State lives in B70_STATE (default <repo>/state): the image, per-family overlays, the trellis-serve checkout, caches,
expert stores, logs. B70_ROOTFS points at an already unpacked image instead; B70_TRELLIS_SRC at a trellis-serve
checkout to use as is (development).
"""
